TITLE:: PltFilter
summary:: Frequency response as a Bode plot, magnitude and phase
categories:: Libraries>PlotLib
related:: Overviews/PlotLib, Classes/SOS, Classes/PltSpectrum

DESCRIPTION::
Magnitude in dB and phase in degrees against log frequency. Several responses can
be overlaid and compared, which is the point: a filter is easy to hear and hard to
picture, and two settings of the same filter are hard to compare any other way.

code::scopeResponse:: exists and is quicker for a glance. This one has axes, a
phase panel, overlays, and needs no server when the coefficients are known.

note::
Coefficients are SuperCollider's link::Classes/SOS:: order, where
code::out = a0*x + a1*x1 + a2*x2 + b1*y1 + b2*y2::, so the denominator is
code::1 - b1 z^-1 - b2 z^-2:: with the sign already carried in the b terms. A
biquad written for the usual textbook convention needs its recursive terms negated.
::

CLASSMETHODS::

METHOD:: new
argument:: coeffs
code::[a0, a1, a2, b1, b2]::
argument:: label
Shown in the legend. Made from the coefficients if left out.
argument:: sampleRate
argument:: title
argument:: points
argument:: width
argument:: height

METHOD:: fromImpulseResponse
A response measured or rendered elsewhere.

METHOD:: fromFunction
A UGen graph, measured by sending an impulse through it on the server. The graph
takes its input as the first argument. Answers through code::action::.
code::
PltFilter.fromFunction({ |in| RLPF.ar(in, 800, 0.2) }, action: { |p| p.front });
::

METHOD:: biquadResponse
The response of one SOS section at the given frequencies: code::[magnitudes,
phases]::, phases in radians. Evaluated on the unit circle, no server needed.

METHOD:: impulseResponse
The same from an impulse response: one DFT term per requested frequency, rather
than an FFT and interpolation, because the points are log spaced and an FFT gives
linear bins.

METHOD:: logFreqs
Log spaced frequencies, so a Bode plot has points where the eye needs them.

INSTANCEMETHODS::

METHOD:: add
Overlay another response from coefficients.
METHOD:: addImpulseResponse
Overlay one from an impulse response.
METHOD:: magnitudeAt
The magnitude at one frequency, in dB.
METHOD:: showPhase
The phase panel, on by default.
METHOD:: minHz
METHOD:: maxHz
Clamped to nyquist.
METHOD:: floorDb
METHOD:: ceilDb
A resonant biquad peaks at about its Q, so leave headroom: 24 dB by default.
METHOD:: curves
METHOD:: freqs
METHOD:: sampleRate
METHOD:: panelGap
METHOD:: showLabels

EXAMPLES::
code::
// a two point averager, a difference filter and a delay
(
f = PltFilter([0.5, 0.5, 0, 0, 0], "averager", 48000, "two point filters");
f.add([1, -1, 0, 0, 0], "difference");
f.add([0, 1, 0, 0, 0], "one sample delay");
f.front;
)

// the same cutoff at three resonances
(
~rbj = { |freq, q|
	var w0 = 2pi * freq / 48000;
	var alpha = sin(w0) / (2 * q);
	var b0 = (1 - cos(w0)) / 2, b1 = 1 - cos(w0);
	var a0 = 1 + alpha, a1 = -2 * cos(w0), a2 = 1 - alpha;
	[b0 / a0, b1 / a0, b0 / a0, a1.neg / a0, a2.neg / a0]
};
f = PltFilter(~rbj.value(800, 0.707), "Q 0.707", 48000, "lowpass at 800 Hz");
f.add(~rbj.value(800, 2), "Q 2");
f.add(~rbj.value(800, 8), "Q 8");
f.front;
)

// measured from a UGen graph
s.boot;
PltFilter.fromFunction({ |in| BPF.ar(in, 1000, 0.1) }, action: { |p| p.front });
::
